{"content_id":"CL-FLD-CABLE-001-OWNERSHIP","domain_id_primary":"D-FLD","domain_ids_secondary":["D-AUD","D-LTG","D-VID","D-ELC"],"content_type":"boundary","route_file":"courses/field-skill-over-under-cable-coiling.html","source_data_file":"scripts/course-data-field.mjs","course_id":"C-FLD-CABLE-COIL","tier_learning":"T2","responsibility_band":"R1","authority_class":"A1","module_identifier":"1","lesson_identifier":"Start With the Assignment","block_identifier":"assignment-ownership","question_identifier":"q1","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"A general stagehand confirms the cable owner, release state, handling method and destination before coiling; appearance alone does not authorize disconnection, repatching, testing, repair or handling of live/show-critical lines.","content_classification":"safety_boundary","safety_criticality":"high","authority_implication":"assigned_support","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Transferable work-control boundary; technical cable authority remains with responsible department/employer."}
{"content_id":"CL-FLD-CABLE-002-INSPECTION","domain_id_primary":"D-FLD","domain_ids_secondary":["D-AUD","D-LTG","D-VID"],"content_type":"claim","route_file":"courses/field-skill-over-under-cable-coiling.html","source_data_file":"scripts/course-data-field.mjs","course_id":"C-FLD-CABLE-COIL","tier_learning":"T2","responsibility_band":"R1","authority_class":"A1","module_identifier":"2","lesson_identifier":"Inspect Before You Coil","block_identifier":"inspection-report","question_identifier":null,"visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"The learner checks for obvious visible damage, route conflict, unclear ownership or abnormal resistance and reports those conditions rather than attempting repair, cleaning, continuity testing or technical diagnosis.","content_classification":"cross_source_pattern","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"assigned_support","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Exact cable/connector inspection criteria remain product/family specific."}
{"content_id":"CL-FLD-CABLE-003-OVERUNDER","domain_id_primary":"D-FLD","domain_ids_secondary":["D-AUD"],"content_type":"claim","route_file":"courses/field-skill-over-under-cable-coiling.html","source_data_file":"scripts/course-data-field.mjs","course_id":"C-FLD-CABLE-COIL","tier_learning":"T2","responsibility_band":"R1","authority_class":"A1","module_identifier":"3","lesson_identifier":"Form Relaxed Alternating Loops","block_identifier":"over-under-concept","question_identifier":"q3","visual_identifier":"V-FLD-CABLE-OVERUNDER-SEQUENCE","learner_facing_text":"Over-under is a common handling method for many flexible production/audio cables because alternating loop orientation manages accumulated twist; the responsible technician/manufacturer controls whether the method and coil diameter apply to the actual cable.","content_classification":"source_backed_instruction","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"assigned_support","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Method concept is source-backed; exact hand technique/diameter is not universal across all cable families."}
{"content_id":"CL-FLD-CABLE-004-EXCEPTIONS","domain_id_primary":"D-FLD","domain_ids_secondary":["D-AUD","D-VID","D-ELC"],"content_type":"boundary","route_file":"courses/field-skill-over-under-cable-coiling.html","source_data_file":"scripts/course-data-field.mjs","course_id":"C-FLD-CABLE-COIL","tier_learning":"T2","responsibility_band":"R1","authority_class":"A1","module_identifier":"4","lesson_identifier":"Secure, Stage, and Know the Exceptions","block_identifier":"cable-specific-limits","question_identifier":"q4","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"Fiber/optical, reel/drum, multicore, feeder and other sensitive or unfamiliar cable assemblies can have product-specific bend/storage/handling limits; cable-specific instructions override a generic hand-coil habit.","content_classification":"manufacturer_or_model_procedure","safety_criticality":"high","authority_implication":"assigned_support","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Specific procedures remain manufacturer/department controlled; course teaches recognition and stop/ask boundary."}
{"content_id":"CL-FLD-CABLE-005-PRACTICESTATE","domain_id_primary":"D-FLD","domain_ids_secondary":["D-EVD"],"content_type":"boundary","route_file":"courses/field-skill-over-under-cable-coiling.html","source_data_file":"scripts/course-data-field.mjs","course_id":"C-FLD-CABLE-COIL","tier_learning":"T2","responsibility_band":"R1","authority_class":"A2","module_identifier":"5","lesson_identifier":"Prepare for Field Observation","block_identifier":"observed-practice-state","question_identifier":"q5","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"Observed practice on one identified cable records performance on that named cable/method/condition; it does not automatically transfer to every cable family or create employer/department authorization.","content_classification":"safety_boundary","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"observed_task_only","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Matches Crew Blueprint A2 observed-task state and preserves A3+ as external."}
{"content_id":"Q-FLD-CABLE-Q1","domain_id_primary":"D-FLD","domain_ids_secondary":["D-EVD"],"content_type":"question","route_file":"courses/field-skill-over-under-cable-coiling.html","source_data_file":"scripts/course-data-field.mjs","course_id":"C-FLD-CABLE-COIL","tier_learning":"T2","responsibility_band":"R1","authority_class":"A1","module_identifier":"1","lesson_identifier":"Start With the Assignment","block_identifier":"quiz","question_identifier":"q1","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"A cable reaches the learner during strike without confirmed release. Correct answer: confirm release and ownership with the responsible technician before handling it.","content_classification":"assessment_prompt","safety_criticality":"high","authority_implication":"assigned_support","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":null}
{"content_id":"QR-FLD-CABLE-Q1","domain_id_primary":"D-FLD","domain_ids_secondary":["D-EVD"],"content_type":"answer_rationale","route_file":"courses/field-skill-over-under-cable-coiling.html","source_data_file":"scripts/course-data-field.mjs","course_id":"C-FLD-CABLE-COIL","tier_learning":"T2","responsibility_band":"R1","authority_class":"A1","module_identifier":"1","lesson_identifier":"Start With the Assignment","block_identifier":"quiz-coaching","question_identifier":"q1","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"Nearby equipment can appear idle while the cable remains technically owned or in service; release/ownership comes from the responsible work process, not appearance.","content_classification":"crew_blueprint_framework","safety_criticality":"high","authority_implication":"assigned_support","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Derived from CL-FLD-CABLE-001-OWNERSHIP."}
{"content_id":"Q-FLD-CABLE-Q2","domain_id_primary":"D-FLD","domain_ids_secondary":["D-EVD"],"content_type":"question","route_file":"courses/field-skill-over-under-cable-coiling.html","source_data_file":"scripts/course-data-field.mjs","course_id":"C-FLD-CABLE-COIL","tier_learning":"T2","responsibility_band":"R1","authority_class":"A1","module_identifier":"3","lesson_identifier":"Form Relaxed Alternating Loops","block_identifier":"quiz","question_identifier":"q2","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"A cable resists the expected coil shape. Correct answer: do not force it; relax the handling and ask whether the directed method or diameter applies to this cable.","content_classification":"assessment_prompt","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"assigned_support","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Tests stop/ask judgment, not force/twist technique."}
{"content_id":"QR-FLD-CABLE-Q2","domain_id_primary":"D-FLD","domain_ids_secondary":["D-EVD"],"content_type":"answer_rationale","route_file":"courses/field-skill-over-under-cable-coiling.html","source_data_file":"scripts/course-data-field.mjs","course_id":"C-FLD-CABLE-COIL","tier_learning":"T2","responsibility_band":"R1","authority_class":"A1","module_identifier":"3","lesson_identifier":"Form Relaxed Alternating Loops","block_identifier":"quiz-coaching","question_identifier":"q2","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"Resistance can reflect natural lay, stiffness, stored twist or a cable-specific handling limit; the learner does not force the cable into a generic pattern.","content_classification":"cross_source_pattern","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"assigned_support","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Derived from CL-FLD-CABLE-003/004."}
{"content_id":"Q-FLD-CABLE-Q3","domain_id_primary":"D-FLD","domain_ids_secondary":["D-AUD","D-EVD"],"content_type":"question","route_file":"courses/field-skill-over-under-cable-coiling.html","source_data_file":"scripts/course-data-field.mjs","course_id":"C-FLD-CABLE-COIL","tier_learning":"T2","responsibility_band":"R1","authority_class":"A1","module_identifier":"3","lesson_identifier":"Form Relaxed Alternating Loops","block_identifier":"quiz","question_identifier":"q3","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"Why is over-under useful for many flexible production cables? Correct answer: alternating loop orientation manages accumulated twist; it does not make every cable identical or eliminate cable-specific rules.","content_classification":"assessment_prompt","safety_criticality":"low","authority_implication":"assigned_support","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":null}
{"content_id":"QR-FLD-CABLE-Q3","domain_id_primary":"D-FLD","domain_ids_secondary":["D-AUD","D-EVD"],"content_type":"answer_rationale","route_file":"courses/field-skill-over-under-cable-coiling.html","source_data_file":"scripts/course-data-field.mjs","course_id":"C-FLD-CABLE-COIL","tier_learning":"T2","responsibility_band":"R1","authority_class":"A1","module_identifier":"3","lesson_identifier":"Form Relaxed Alternating Loops","block_identifier":"quiz-coaching","question_identifier":"q3","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"The alternating lay manages twist in successive loops and can support cleaner deployment on compatible flexible cables; actual cable instructions still control.","content_classification":"source_backed_instruction","safety_criticality":"low","authority_implication":"assigned_support","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Derived from CL-FLD-CABLE-003-OVERUNDER."}
{"content_id":"Q-FLD-CABLE-Q4","domain_id_primary":"D-FLD","domain_ids_secondary":["D-VID","D-EVD"],"content_type":"question","route_file":"courses/field-skill-over-under-cable-coiling.html","source_data_file":"scripts/course-data-field.mjs","course_id":"C-FLD-CABLE-COIL","tier_learning":"T2","responsibility_band":"R1","authority_class":"A1","module_identifier":"4","lesson_identifier":"Secure, Stage, and Know the Exceptions","block_identifier":"quiz","question_identifier":"q4","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"A fiber assembly arrives on its original reel. Correct answer: follow the responsible technician/manufacturer handling method rather than automatically converting it to a hand-coiled over-under method.","content_classification":"assessment_prompt","safety_criticality":"high","authority_implication":"assigned_support","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":null}
{"content_id":"QR-FLD-CABLE-Q4","domain_id_primary":"D-FLD","domain_ids_secondary":["D-VID","D-EVD"],"content_type":"answer_rationale","route_file":"courses/field-skill-over-under-cable-coiling.html","source_data_file":"scripts/course-data-field.mjs","course_id":"C-FLD-CABLE-COIL","tier_learning":"T2","responsibility_band":"R1","authority_class":"A1","module_identifier":"4","lesson_identifier":"Secure, Stage, and Know the Exceptions","block_identifier":"quiz-coaching","question_identifier":"q4","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"Fiber and other sensitive cable assemblies can have product-specific minimum bend/coiling/storage requirements, so generic handling habits do not override manufacturer/department instructions.","content_classification":"manufacturer_or_model_procedure","safety_criticality":"high","authority_implication":"assigned_support","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Derived from CL-FLD-CABLE-004-EXCEPTIONS."}
{"content_id":"Q-FLD-CABLE-Q5","domain_id_primary":"D-FLD","domain_ids_secondary":["D-EVD"],"content_type":"question","route_file":"courses/field-skill-over-under-cable-coiling.html","source_data_file":"scripts/course-data-field.mjs","course_id":"C-FLD-CABLE-COIL","tier_learning":"T2","responsibility_band":"R1","authority_class":"A2","module_identifier":"5","lesson_identifier":"Prepare for Field Observation","block_identifier":"quiz","question_identifier":"q5","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"What does observed practice on one identified cable establish? Correct answer: performance of that named task under those conditions, not universal cable competence or authority.","content_classification":"assessment_prompt","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"observed_task_only","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":null}
{"content_id":"QR-FLD-CABLE-Q5","domain_id_primary":"D-FLD","domain_ids_secondary":["D-EVD"],"content_type":"answer_rationale","route_file":"courses/field-skill-over-under-cable-coiling.html","source_data_file":"scripts/course-data-field.mjs","course_id":"C-FLD-CABLE-COIL","tier_learning":"T2","responsibility_band":"R1","authority_class":"A2","module_identifier":"5","lesson_identifier":"Prepare for Field Observation","block_identifier":"quiz-coaching","question_identifier":"q5","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"Observed practice records the named equipment/method/conditions. Transfer to other cable families and employer/department authorization remain separate evidence states.","content_classification":"crew_blueprint_framework","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"observed_task_only","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Derived from CL-FLD-CABLE-005-PRACTICESTATE."}